# cross-lib-decision-split — Lib A (the referring policy library).
library "Root".

// Root delegates to the sibling Shared library's decision via
// `use decision "Shared"."Sub Triage"`. Shared is AUTO-SPLIT (it has
// concept-level `code is` + a decision → interface split), so Shared's SOURCE
// name no longer exists as an emitted CQL library. The question this fixture
// pins: does a cross-lib `use decision` into a split library resolve (via the
// policy-id-scoped Decision PlanDefinition) or fail the split-library guard?
//
// Root itself has NO concept-level `code is` (only ONE library per policy may),
// so its condition is a RecordSource `coded from` concept.

terminology "Mild Crohns VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vs/mild-crohns`.

concept "Mild Crohns":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- coded from "Mild Crohns VS".

decision "Triage Crohns":
- when "Mild Crohns" then use decision "Shared"."Sub Triage".
